# Recall API (Python)

~44k lines in `app/` excluding tests. Product domains are migrating from horizontal
routers/services folders into `modules/<domain>/`; infrastructure stays in core/gateways/repositories.

- async/await for all IO; full type hints; Pydantic v2 schemas
- Config / feature flags via `app/core/config.py` — never read `os.environ` elsewhere
- Chat loop in `app/services/chat/`; quota/lock via `turn_resources`
- Migrated modules own their API, service, models/schemas, jobs, scheduler, and tool adapter
- Jobs: a module job or `background/handlers.py` registers; `core/jobs.py` is the queue only
- MCP tools: module-owned or legacy `services/mcp/` adapters register via `gateways/mcp/`
- Background jobs: wrap body in try/except; never raise into chat path
- Mock LiteLLM, Redis, Google, Neon in tests — zero real network calls
- Format/lint: `uv run ruff format . && uv run ruff check .`
- Coverage target 80%+ (`pytest --cov=app --cov-fail-under=80`)
